Vikram and Betal: The Two Brothers

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there were two brothers,” said Betal. “The elder brother was greedy, and the younger one was kind and honest.”

One day, their father gave them some land and money to share equally.

The elder brother secretly took more than his share.

The younger brother did not complain and continued to work hard.

After some time, the younger brother became successful because of his honesty and effort.

The elder brother, however, lost his wealth due to his greed.

One day, the elder brother came to his younger brother for help.

The younger brother welcomed him kindly and shared everything.

Betal then asked, “Vikram, who is truly rich?”

Vikram replied, “The younger brother is truly rich because he has kindness and honesty.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

True wealth lies in kindness and honesty.
